From c4ed16a58ba29aa1a0773fff4c3b9e9a330af7d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nadelacruz-00 <323917690+nadelacruz-00@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:27:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] staging: qca-wifi-host-cmn: hif: make
 hif_exec_napi_kill() idempotent
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The WLAN idle shutdown (cnss, about 250 ms after NetworkManager takes
the interface down, for example on PrepareForSleep before a suspend)
kills each of the 18 hif ext groups more than once per shutdown.
hif_exec_napi_kill() deletes the napi and frees its dummy netdev on the
first call, but napi.dev still points at the freed netdev. On this
kernel netif_napi_del() and napi_disable() take netdev_lock(napi->dev),
so the next kill locks freed memory and oopses. The tablet crashes on
the third idle shutdown after boot, which in practice freezes the next
suspend:

  Internal error: Oops: 0000000096000004 [#1] SMP
  pc : __mutex_lock.constprop.0+0xa8/0x8c8
  Call trace:
   mutex_lock
   hif_exec_napi_kill [wlan]
   hif_exec_kill [wlan]
   hif_pci_disable_isr [wlan]
   hif_ce_stop [wlan]
   htc_stop [wlan]
   hdd_wlan_stop_modules [wlan]
   hdd_psoc_idle_shutdown [wlan]
   cnss_pci_call_driver_remove [cnss2]
   cnss_pci_dev_shutdown [cnss2]

The first kill already NULLs n_ctx->netdev after freeing it, so return
early when it is NULL. The second and later kills of a context become
no-ops.

Tested on a OnePlus Pad 3 (SM8750): five Wi-Fi off/on cycles, each
with an idle shutdown and restart, and repeated s2idle cycles, all
without an oops. Without the change the third idle shutdown after
boot oopses every time.

Fixes: e1215bf27f98 ("staging: qcacld-3.0 — build the WCN7880 WLAN driver in-tree")
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/staging/qca-wifi-host-cmn/hif/src/hif_exec.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/qca-wifi-host-cmn/hif/src/hif_exec.c b/drivers/staging/qca-wifi-host-cmn/hif/src/hif_exec.c
index 11105eb05..223c17919 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/qca-wifi-host-cmn/hif/src/hif_exec.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/qca-wifi-host-cmn/hif/src/hif_exec.c
@@ -911,6 +911,15 @@ static void hif_exec_napi_kill(struct hif_exec_context *ctx)
 	struct hif_napi_exec_context *n_ctx = hif_exec_get_napi(ctx);
 	int irq_ind;
 
+	/*
+	 * erhai: a second kill of the same context must be a no-op. The first
+	 * kill deletes the napi and frees its dummy netdev, but napi.dev still
+	 * points at the freed netdev, and netif_napi_del() and napi_disable()
+	 * take netdev_lock(napi->dev): a second kill locks freed memory.
+	 */
+	if (!n_ctx->netdev)
+		return;
+
 	if (ctx->inited) {
 		qdf_napi_disable(&n_ctx->napi);
 		ctx->inited = 0;
-- 
